---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import BrowserFrame from "@/components/BrowserFrame.astro";
import WorkMedia from "@/components/work/WorkMedia.astro";
import { DATA } from "@/data/resume";

const externalUrl = "https://catconnectionsnyc.org";
const linkedInUrl = DATA.contact.social.LinkedIn.url;
---

<Layout
  title="Founder Story"
  description="The story of Cat Connections NYC, a cat rescue I founded and ran in Astoria, Queens."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <a href="/about" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">
      &larr; About
    </a>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class="mt-8">
      <span class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground">Founder Story</span>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl">Cat Connections NYC</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl text-lg text-muted-foreground">
        A grassroots cat rescue I founded and ran in Astoria, Queens - adoption, community-cat
        support, and fundraising built from nothing.
      </p>
      <a
        href={externalUrl}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md bg-foreground px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-background hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
      >
        Visit Cat Connections NYC &rarr;
      </a>
    </header>

    <BrowserFrame class="mt-10 aspect-[16/10] w-full">
      <WorkMedia title="Cat Connections NYC website" thumbnailVideo="/work/cat-connections-nyc.mp4" class="size-full" />
    </BrowserFrame>

    <div class="mt-14 flex flex-col gap-12">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">The Story</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          I founded Cat Connections NYC, a grassroots cat rescue based in Astoria, Queens,
          where I served as technical lead, fundraising director, and social media manager from the start.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          It started after I volunteered at Astoria Cat Rescue, where I met a group of people who
          wanted to form something of their own. We set out together, and my original vision was a
          foster-based rescue that would one day grow into a cat café. It turned out to be far
          less simple than that.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">What It Became</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          I built the organization's digital presence from nothing. The first website ran on
          WordPress, with custom PHP that pulled adoptable cats through the API of Animals First,
          our animal database software at the time. I later migrated the site to Webflow CMS, with
          a structured content model so adoptable and adopted cats, campaigns, and impact stories
          could be updated without a developer.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          Behind the site, I implemented two animal management systems - first Animals First, then
          Shelterluv - and built the rescue's complex foster, adoption, and volunteer
          applications.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          On the fundraising side, I ran campaigns across multiple platforms at once - Raisely,
          Zeffy, GoFundMe, Reddit, Instagram, and Facebook - including community-driven posts on
          Reddit, a channel most nonprofit sites ignore entirely. That effort raised $18,000 in
          about six months, including a Fidelity Corporate Giving match.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          Around 50 cats found adoptive homes through Cat Connections NYC. We also took in many
          cats with heavy medical needs - Mr. Blinks, Stevie, McLean, Charlie, Felix, and many
          others. Most needed expensive dental treatment, several dealt with ulcers, and Mr.
          Blinks had an overgrown conjunctiva that left his eyes half closed and required
          corrective surgery.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">Why It Ended</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          Rescue work is overwhelming, and as I had less and less time, I gradually became less
          involved. The other members had their own lives and responsibilities that kept them from
          participating fully, too. Eventually my family moved to Upstate New York for my
          husband's job, and I paused my collaboration with Cat Connections NYC.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          The group was quiet for a while, but it's now making a small comeback, with new people
          joining.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">Looking Back</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          I learned a lot about animal welfare - how trapping works, what medical treatment really
          costs, how to build and write successful fundraising campaigns, and how to run the
          software behind a rescue, from different CRMs to beautiful, efficient donation forms.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-foreground">
          I also learned how hard rescue is, how demanding its day-to-day operations are, and how
          quickly small conflicts can escalate into something bigger.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            href={linkedInUrl}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted transition-colors"
          >
            Read more about me &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
